1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,340
The rumored swim-trunks
detective has appeared.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,340
Above all,

3
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:32,840
What is it, Chief?

4
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:38,580
Today, I want to entrust you with
an important and special mission.

5
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,580
Mission?

6
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:41,980
The one who can carry
out this duty admirably

7
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:44,180
even among all the many
officers at Katsushika Precinct,

8
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:47,160
there's no one but you, Ryotsu.

9
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:51,680
I have a bad feeling about this.

10
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,980
It's a joint investigation
with headquarters.

11
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:56,380
With veteran Detective Kitano and you,

12
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:58,480
you're going to be partners.

13
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,680
Detective Kitano.

14
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,820
Do you know him, Terai?

15
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:03,900
Well, only by name.

16
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:10,340
Isn't he supposed to be the best elite detective at headquarters,
with a 100% arrest rate?

17
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:11,900
That's amazing, Ryo-chan.

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:15,160
To be chosen as the partner
of such an elite detective!

19
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:16,340
Here you are, Chief.

20
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,700
Mm, thank you.

21
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:19,600
But why me?

22
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:21,793
Well, you see,

23
00:01:21,843 --> 00:01:26,660
headquarters asked us to send the most
physically fit officer from Katsushika Station,

24
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:29,320
so I recommended you.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,140
Well, that makes sense.

26
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:31,800
What did you say?

27
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:32,280
[beep]

28
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:33,860
Besides,

29
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,420
depending on your conduct on the job,
headquarters is considering

30
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:39,600
promoting you, apparently.

31
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,180
Promotion?

32
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:45,520
Rich folks have their own tastes

33
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,520
Way to go, senior!

34
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,960
It's a chance, you know.

35
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,460
If it's a promotion without an exam,

36
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,460
Ryo-san's got a shot too, right?

37
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,120
What's that supposed to mean?

38
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:59,180
They should be arriving any moment now.

39
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,760
Well, I'll be taking my leave now.

40
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,780
You're leaving already?

41
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,000
At least introduce me first.

42
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,376
No, well, you see, I'm...

43
00:02:08,426 --> 00:02:11,020
I've got a lot of things to
take care of from here on.

44
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,736
Hey, Chief,

45
00:02:12,786 --> 00:02:16,320
Hold on a second!

46
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:20,200
Listen, whatever you do,
do what Detective Kitano says.

47
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:22,020
Follow his orders without argument, got it?

48
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:26,840
Chief! What do you mean, "that"?

49
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:27,980
Chief!

50
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:32,520
He sure left in a hurry, didn't he.

51
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,100
He's here, he's here, Nakagawa!

52
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,060
Kushi! Kushi!

53
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:39,560
Yes.

54
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,320
Ryo-chan, your tie is crooked.

55
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,440
Thanks.

56
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,080
Listen, Ryo-san.

57
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,180
First impressions are important
in situations like this.

58
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,920
You have to look sharp.

59
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:55,900
I'm getting nervous.

60
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,420
I wondered what on earth he was
going to pull out all of a sudden.

61
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:26,840
B-business card?

62
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,520
I'm the detective who was sent here.

63
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
At headquarters, I'm known as the Swim-Trunks Detective.
On the back is my profile, up to yesterday.

64
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,600
Nice to meet you. I'm your partner.

65
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,580
I can't read it without a magnifying glass.

66
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:53,120
You're asking why I'm only in swim trunks? Well, sharp as ever.
As expected, my criminal arrest rate is 100%.

67
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,200
You don't have anything else to ask, do you?

68
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,660
Very well. I'll answer.

69
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:01,320
All animals other than humans are naked.

70
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:04,500
In other words, this is the natural form.

71
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:09,180
You haven't noticed that your uniforms
have robbed your bodies of their freedom.

72
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,600
You, try bending your body backward.

73
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,620
L-like this?

74
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,040
What, is that all?

75
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,880
How much further can I possibly go?

76
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,440
Bend back at least this much.

77
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:29,040
When you're naked like this, clothing's burden doesn't hinder the body's movement,
so you can move freely.

78
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,220
Dangerous guy.

79
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,680
But a naked body has no limits.

80
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:40,300
Humans' latent motor nerves are pushed
to their utmost limits by being naked,

81
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:44,860
which means you can make the quick,
agile movements needed to arrest criminals.

82
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:46,700
Can you do that just by getting naked?

83
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,240
Throw me.

84
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:50,640
Come on.

85
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:53,980
Well then, without holding back.

86
00:04:59,160 --> 00:04:59,520
What?

87
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:03,160
Damn, it's too slippery to grip!

88
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:06,340
A naked body is impossible to get a hold of.

89
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:12,240
Are you all right, Ryo-san?

90
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:15,940
This is a secret oil passed
down in my family from the north.

91
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,180
The faint scent that drifts about

92
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,640
also has a calming effect that soothes
the agitated hearts of criminals.

93
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:26,520
Everything is rational.

94
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:27,480
Is that so?

95
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:32,380
In other words, this is the
natural form a detective should take.

96
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,520
Before asking me why
I'm wearing swim trunks,

97
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:40,260
you should ask yourselves why
you wear such heavy uniforms.

98
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,280
Reconsider it for yourselves.

99
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:45,320
It's not because we're embarrassed.

100
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:45,940
Ryo-san.

101
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:46,820
What is it?

102
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,200
If you upset the detective
from headquarters here,

103
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,080
my promotion is on the line, you know.

104
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,020
O-oh, I see.

105
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,600
And one more thing.

106
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,460
There's also the,

107
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:55,900
both of you,

108
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,360
by not decorating your person,

109
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:01,180
you can speak from the
heart even with criminals.

110
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:02,580
That's all.

111
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,680
Any other questions?

112
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:04,800
Yes.

113
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:06,100
Ryotsu-kun.

114
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:08,000
What's that strapped to your leg?

115
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:10,080
It's a backup pistol.

116
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,260
But normally,

117
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:12,880
that's true,

118
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:15,300
detectives who wear clothes

119
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,240
hide their backup guns.

120
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:21,900
That would be too obvious,
and you'd stand out even more.

121
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,680
Criminals don't open up,
they're wary of you!

122
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,140
Old man.

123
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,100
Sure.

124
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,180
But.

125
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:32,200
I hate secrets.

126
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,020
What's that supposed to mean?

127
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:38,100
Even if the opponent is a violent criminal,

128
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,880
I treat them with sincerity.

129
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,720
That's my policy.

130
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:43,040
P-perfect.

131
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:44,920
It's logical in every way.

132
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:45,520
Where?

133
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,720
Why would you need that?

134
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:56,800
It's time to refuel.

135
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:02,340
I make it a rule to eat on time,
no matter the circumstances.

136
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,520
How about you all join me?

137
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,660
No thank you.

138
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:13,240
Damn it,
the Chief knew about this and ran off!

139
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,740
By the way, my partner, Ryotsu,

140
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,440
This way.

141
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:22,520
Unfortunately, Ryotsu is off sick today.

142
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:24,980
Sick with what?

143
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,200
Well, that can't be helped.

144
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:30,780
Then I'll choose from the
members who are here now.

145
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:32,520
This man is Ryotsu.

146
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,100
What did I do to deserve this?

147
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:41,800
Swim trunks and a tie are our formal attire.

148
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:47,580
As my partner, you'll follow my policy 120%.

149
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,600
Understood?

150
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:53,440
If I go out dressed like this, I'll
get arrested before I catch the criminal.

151
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:56,360
Ryotsu, your butt is sagging.

152
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,880
Tighten it up more.

153
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,200
How?

154
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:00,080
Like this.

155
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,440
Like this?

156
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,500
No, no, watch.

157
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,200
Again with the underwear?

158
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,520
Like this.

159
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,400
W-wow!

160
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:18,000
This is a move you could
never do with your clothes on.

161
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,420
Even if you can do it,
it's no use to anyone.

162
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:25,520
That's not ours.

163
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,400
It's not my cell phone either.

164
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,400
That's mine.

165
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,760
At this rate,
pigeons and bankokuchi will show up too!

166
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,620
No way.

167
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,500
What?

168
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:38,600
The serial robber has taken a hostage...

169
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,100
Serial robber?

170
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,500
Got it, heading to the scene right away.

171
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,320
Let's go, Ryotsu.

172
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:53,920
For an elite detective,
you're too much of a freak.

173
00:08:56,880 --> 00:09:00,080
The culprit has taken a student hostage
and is holed up in a girls' school.

174
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,120
Our long investigation finally paid
off and we've cornered the culprit,

175
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:06,220
but who would have thought
it would come to this.

176
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:06,660
Fine.

177
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,200
Kitano-kun, that's all well and good, but

178
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,200
in this cold,
we can't move the way we want to.

179
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:16,500
I see. Then I'll lend you my trunks.

180
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,140
The winter cold really gets to you,
doesn't it.

181
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:21,620
I always wear these on stakeouts too.

182
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,980
Clothes for people who hate clothes.

183
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:29,640
Hey!

184
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:30,740
Make a move!

185
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:33,060
I'll cut you to pieces
and make you pay for this!

186
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,640
Shut up!

187
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,760
If you come any closer,

188
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:39,560
don't blame me if something
happens to this guy!

189
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,040
Where's Perry?

190
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,340
Did you get the hundred million yen?

191
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,240
Even if you do that, you won't get away.

192
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:51,820
Shut up already!

193
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,340
You're here.

194
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:09,060
W-w-w-what, what is that?

195
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:11,220
Kitano-kun, we've been waiting for you!

196
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,120
Chief, what's the situation?

197
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:21,460
It's no good. The culprit won't
even listen to our persuasion.

198
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,920
The hostage is nearing their limit,
both mentally and physically.

199
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:31,340
How long do you plan to keep us waiting?

200
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:33,260
Hurry up and die.

201
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,020
He's getting awfully worked up, isn't he?

202
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,080
Understood.

203
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:41,080
Leave the rest to me and pull the
riot police back to the school gate.

204
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:41,880
Understood.

205
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:44,000
All units, retreat to the school gate.

206
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,140
Let's go, Ryotsu.

207
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:49,020
Kitano-kun, put on your bulletproof vest.

208
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,800
I don't need it.

209
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:53,880
I'm the Swim-Trunks Detective.

210
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,580
No, no, I told you I don't need it.

211
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,460
No matter how you think about it,

212
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:02,080
Ryotsu, follow right behind me.

213
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,880
"Follow right behind me," he says.

214
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:03,900
Wh-wait, hold on a second.

215
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:04,080
Got it!

216
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,760
W-w-what is that guy?!

217
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,160
Stay back!

218
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:19,000
That's reckless! Let's leave this to him!

219
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,260
Wh-what?

220
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:25,960
You're his partner, aren't you?
What are you doing running away?

221
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,520
No, I'm only - just me!

222
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,400
Th-that's crazy!

223
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,340
Dangerous! Dangerous!

224
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:35,260
Help!

225
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:36,980
Stop firing!

226
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:39,440
Look, we're unarmed.

227
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:42,520
We only came to talk.

228
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:46,280
Then what's that strapped to your leg?

229
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,060
Busted

230
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:50,880
Of course!

231
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,080
There, that should do it.

232
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,600
You're not hiding anything else, are you?

233
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:01,100
W-what, what, what is it?

234
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:04,120
No good, no good.

235
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,660
Lucky!

236
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:10,440
I refuel every thirty minutes.

237
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:14,160
Don't you have any sense of tension?

238
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:17,640
Damn it, they're making fun of me!

239
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:20,460
There's nothing to fear.

240
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:22,020
No, I'm angry.

241
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:26,080
Ryotsu, this is your first mission.

242
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,040
I permit you to use this.

243
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,540
A tray?

244
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,580
Damn it, what are you planning to do?

245
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:41,960
Now I'm completely defenseless.

246
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:47,860
What are you doing, Ryotsu?

247
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:51,540
Wait, don't tell me this tray is -

248
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,300
There's no way I can do that.

249
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,660
Ryotsu!

250
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,920
This is a matter of life and death!

251
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,860
Fine, I get it.

252
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,360
So I just have to strip, right?

253
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:09,960
Just take it off.

254
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:16,060
Senpai.

255
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:17,420
Ryo-chan!

256
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,420
Ryo-san!

257
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:27,080
Listen, I'm coming over there now.

258
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:31,440
Calm down and hear me out, will you?

259
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,800
Once upon a time,

260
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,680
in a certain place...

261
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,760
Hey, hey, that's not persuading anyone!

262
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,980
What, what, what?

263
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:46,380
What's with those people?

264
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,800
W-wait, stop!
Tell me about the Nanba-gah pervert!

265
00:13:50,180 --> 00:13:52,960
Shut up! Don't ask me!

266
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,280
Now!

267
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,580
It's going to fall!

268
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:10,080
Frypan key!

269
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:18,960
Detective Kitano

270
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:19,720
Ryotsu

271
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,600
Protect the girl.

272
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,120
Yes.

273
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,720
No, don't come near me!

274
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:28,780
It's all right.

275
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,020
At least I'm more decent
than that guy over there.

276
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:33,580
Ugh, it stinks!

277
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,860
You still intend to resist?

278
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:40,240
To be caught by a detective in the buff,
of all things.

279
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,460
Then you'll never be able to laugh again,
you know.

280
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,240
Aaaaaaah!

281
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,140
Ni

282
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,280
Aaaaaaah!

283
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,680
Aaaaaaah!

284
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:59,640
Eeeeeeh!

285
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:03,920
Aaaaaaah!

286
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:05,900
Yaaay!

287
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:13,980
So in the buff,
I'm the one paying the pants tax?

288
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:23,100
Looks like the scent of the oil worked,
after all.

289
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:26,000
The scent of oil, really? Hey!

290
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:28,520
Ryotsu, what happened to the girl?

291
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:33,180
She got scared and ran under a desk.

292
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,400
There, you're safe now.

293
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,360
All done, miss.

294
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,660
Sorry about that.

295
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:48,160
I was careless, which isn't like me.

296
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,620
How rude of me, in front of a lady.

297
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:53,340
Was my tie crooked?

298
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:54,260
Lower, lower.

299
00:15:57,180 --> 00:15:58,160
It's done.

300
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:01,960
We did it.

301
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:03,600
Here they come.

302
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,540
Isabu!

303
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:07,520
Let's hurry up and head home.

304
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,520
Is everyone all right?

305
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,460
There's surely a rational

306
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:43,180
explanation for this,
of course there isn't, you idiot.

307
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,600
Good work, Ryotsu.

308
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,460
I have nothing more to teach you.

309
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,620
I don't want to be taught anything more.

310
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:57,120
Starting tomorrow,
you're promoted to detective.

311
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:58,820
Mario-san!

312
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:03,100
Putting up with you was worth it after all.

313
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:06,540
And by the way, this is a present for you.

314
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,237
Wearing a tie to match mine,

315
00:17:10,287 --> 00:17:12,600
turn over a new leaf and do your best.

316
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:16,060
Thank you. No, I'm really happy!

317
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,692
Well then, tomorrow at 8:30,

318
00:17:17,742 --> 00:17:20,047
tie it around your most important part,

319
00:17:20,097 --> 00:17:21,780
and come to me.

320
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,000
Give it a name.

321
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,300
Full-Frontal Detective.

322
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,440
Swim-Trunks Detective
and Full-Frontal Detective.

323
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,880
Sounds like we'd make a good pair.

324
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,280
Don't mess with me, you pervert!

325
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:39,700
There's no way that would fly on Golden Live,
you know!

326
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,560
You idiot!

327
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:47,840
Next, I'll take on the
Hyper Elementary School Kid!

